{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And He planted</b>: He had already planted a garden in a place called Eden, on the east side, and now He placed the man in it. The meaning of גן בעדן [garden in Eden] is גן אלהים [garden of Elohim]; the bet serves itself and afterward עמו בעדן בגן אלהים [with Him in Eden, in the garden of Elohim], and similar is מאל אביך ויעזרך [from the El of your father, and He will help you] (Genesis 49:25), and many others." "The heh of האדם [the man] has a sod. So too is found שבט המנשה [the tribe of Manasseh] (Deuteronomy 3:13), הארוני, היבוסי [the Arkite, the Jebusite] (2 Samuel 24:16). And it is also possible for it to be so, because it is a name hewn from אדמה [ground], and it can be both a noun and an adjective."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:46.566372490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}